Z||000000||rprevo||09-19-2000||09:58 PM|||| Anybody know how good this little box<BR>is to the real Horsepower and 1/4 mile<BR>test?<BR> I recently tried with my Carburated<BR>350 v8 and got 225 real b/h/p and when<BR>I did the 1/4 mile test it gave me a<BR>trap spd of 101 mph and a 1/4 mile time<BR>of 13.2.<BR>This was all done on the expressway<BR>late at night.<BR>For those who do not know what I'm talking<BR>about it is a little box that gets mounted<BR>in your car and it determines power by <BR>G-forces .<BR> It was 100 bucks through Summit.<BR>I have never dynoed or ran the car at the<BR>track but was wondering if any one had ever<BR>compared this box to real life.<P>Ray<BR>   <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cooter||09-19-2000||10:57 PM||||I have wanted to buy one for a while now. I don't know if they give an accurate HP number, but you can use it to get a baseline and make some changes and see if you really improved the acceleration or not. Or maybe I just need a precision calibrated ass-O-meter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||09-20-2000||12:35 AM||||I have almost had my g-tech for 2 years now.  I have found it to be pretty accurate.  I did the hp test with my g-tech and I got 128 peak according to the g-tech.  I went to a dyno like a month later and I peaked at 129.  So the g-tech was only off 1 peak hp which is what it claims it is accurate to.<P>I have also taken it to the track and compared it with my timeslips.  G-tech was accurate almost to .010 on a few runs.  Other runs it was off by about .1 but no more then a tenth off.  Mph is high on the g-tech compared to the dragstrip.  This is because the strip averages your speed between a set of lights.  The g-tech measures the speed at the exact end of the qtr mile.<P>Believe what it is telling you cause it is accurate.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000003||80's BOY||09-20-2000||10:10 AM||||my ricer friend let me use his. i only got 100BHP at the rear wheels. is this correct?? 1985 fiero gt 3.1 stroker kit.||||reg||5
